Spec: Project/Domains

Purpose:
  Define the concrete business domains of the SDDRA ecosystem — the
  bounded contexts that make up the system. Each domain represents a
  distinct area of business capability with its own vocabulary, rules,
  and ownership.

Owns:
  Domain definitions
  Domain boundaries
  Domain relationships
  Bounded context mapping

Domains:

  Integration:
    purpose: External system connectivity — banks, MFOs, gamification platforms, notification providers
    bounded_contexts:
      - captainup-gamification (CaptainUp: points, badges, leaderboards, player profiles)
      - pultapaz (Bank/MFO credit integrations)
    owns:
      - Integration configuration (endpoints, auth, field mapping)
      - Pre-check execution (identity validation against external APIs)
      - Request/response field mapping and transformation
      - Status polling and webhook processing
      - Retry and error handling policies
      - Daily limits and rate limiting
      - Gamification event ingestion (point awards, badge unlocks)
      - Player identity mapping (internal user <-> CaptainUp auid)
    shared_kernel:
      - Field mapping engine (internal_field -> external_field, field_path, transforms)
      - Integration conditions (amount, duration, employment status rules)
      - HTTP client abstraction (content-type, auth, timeout)
      - Audit logging (request/response/execution time)
    relationships:
      - uses: Notification
      - uses: EventProcessing
      - uses: Scheduling
      - uses: Gamification

  Gamification:
    purpose: Player engagement system — points, badges, leaderboards, rules
    bounded_contexts:
      - gamification-rules (rule engine for points, badges, achievements)
      - gamification-leaderboard (ranked lists, scopes, caching)
      - gamification-player (player profile, identity, progression)
      - gamification-anticheat (validation, anomaly detection, rollback)
    owns:
      - Rule definitions (points, badges, achievements, campaigns)
      - Rule evaluation engine (async, idempotent, auditable)
      - Player state (balance, badges, streak, level)
      - Leaderboard write and read models
      - Anti-cheat detection and enforcement
      - Real-time event delivery (WebSocket firehose)
      - Time-window aggregation (daily, weekly, monthly)
    shared_kernel:
      - Event envelope (action_performed, user_id, context, timestamp)
      - Correlation ID propagation
      - Daily limit enforcement
      - Audit trail for all gamification actions
    relationships:
      - uses: Integration (external CaptainUp API)
      - uses: EventProcessing (action events, point events)
      - uses: Notification (badge unlock, rank change alerts)
      - uses: Scheduling (batch leaderboard rebuild, badge evaluation)
      - used_by: User (player attributes, progression)

  Notification:
    purpose: Multi-channel outbound messaging — email, SMS, Telegram, Slack
    bounded_contexts:
      - email (Mailgun/SMTP template rendering)
      - sms (provider abstraction)
      - telegram (bot API)
      - slack (webhook-based rich messages)
    owns:
      - Template engine (placeholder replacement, HTML rendering)
      - Provider abstraction (send via configured channel)
      - Daily limits per integration
      - Retry logic for failed sends
    relationships:
      - uses: EventProcessing

  EventProcessing:
    purpose: Event/message intake, dispatch, and lifecycle management
    bounded_contexts:
      - gamification-firehose (CaptainUp real-time events via WebSocket)
      - rabbitmq-consumers (async mail/batch processing)
      - polling-fallback (Supabase DB-based queue)
    owns:
      - Event claiming and deduplication
      - Handler dispatch (service + event_type routing)
      - Retry policy (count, backoff, dead-letter)
      - Correlation ID tracking
      - Batch completion and status updates
      - Gamification event routing (points, badges, leaderboards)
    relationships:
      - uses: Integration
      - uses: Notification
      - uses: Gamification

  Scheduling:
    purpose: Periodic and delayed task execution
    bounded_contexts:
      - gamification-sync (CaptainUp periodic player/leaderboard sync)
      - yii2-delayed-task (pultapaz batch operations)
    owns:
      - Cron job registration and execution
      - Delayed task queue management
      - Batch orchestration (pre-check, sync)
      - Gamification batch jobs (leaderboard rebuild, badge evaluation)
    relationships:
      - uses: Integration
      - uses: EventProcessing
      - uses: Gamification

  User:
    purpose: User identity and profile across internal and external systems
    bounded_contexts:
      - quiz-user (pultapaz — QuizParams, QuizRedirects)
      - gamification-player (CaptainUp — player profile, auid mapping, progression)
      - external-mapping (cross-system user ID mapping)
    owns:
      - User profile data (FIN, phone, name, document)
      - External service user mapping (internal ID -> external ID)
      - User-level daily limits
      - Gamification attributes (level, experience, badges)
    relationships:
      - used_by: Integration
      - used_by: Notification
      - used_by: Gamification

Rules:
  [D1] Each domain MUST have an identifiable bounded context.
  [D2] Domain knowledge MUST remain within its own domain model.
  [D3] Cross-domain communication MUST use explicit contracts.
  [D4] A domain MUST NOT access another domain's internal structures.
  [D5] Shared kernel MUST be explicitly declared and versioned.
  [D6] Domain boundaries MUST align with business capability, not technical layer.
  [D7] A domain MAY span multiple implementations (bounded contexts).
  [D8] Domain relationships MUST be recorded in dependencies.sdd.

Navigation:
  Modules: @modules.sdd
  Flows: @flows.sdd
  Dependencies: @dependencies.sdd
  Architecture: @../architecture/principles.sdd

